 apartment, old and new leases</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>Up about 3%</strong><span class="t">house rents in a year</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 3, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Rents on leases of a year or more, by bedrooms and in ten ZIP codes from Little River to Murrells Inlet.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house rents for about $1,600 a month on a new lease in Horry County outside the Loris, Aynor and Green Sea area. The tenant also pays about $200 a month for power, water and gas. That is the middle rent for houses leased in the last two years: half rent for more, and half for less.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An apartment or condo rents for about $1,100 a month with one bedroom and about $1,150 with two, plus about $100 of utilities. Those apartment figures count leases old and new, so a new lease costs more than that.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">An agent works out the rent for one house before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Ask an agent</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#by-bedrooms" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">By bedrooms</a></li><li><a href="#new-leases" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">New leases</a></li><li><a href="#by-area" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">By area</a></li><li><a href="#up-or-down" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Are rents rising</a></li><li><a href="#best-month" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Best month</a></li><li><a href="#your-house" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What will my house rent for</a></li><li><a href="#fair-market-rent" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Fair market rent</a></li><li><a href="#raising-the-rent" style="display:block;padding:.65