+Carrying the fee and tax of the typical oceanfront two-bedroom, the average rental would fall about $2,100 short. A rental at the top-quarter mark, rented all year, would cover them and keep about $9,600 for insurance and the loan. A condo pays when it rents like the busier listings, or when its fee and tax are lower.
+His own numbers, not a promise
+A friend of ours ran a hotel in Boston. When he retired, a house sale and his savings bought three condos in one oceanfront building here.
+He had about $100,000 saved and sold his Massachusetts house for about $450,000. The three condos gross about $120,000 a year, an average of about $40,000 a condo, and roughly half of it is profit. He now helps manage fourteen units.
