brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Carolina Forest</a>. It is the master-planned inland corridor, the HOAs require long leases rather than nightly stays, and tenant demand follows the school attendance zones.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want the easiest property to buy, rent and resell</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Myrtle Beach</a> or <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">North Myrtle Beach</a>. They hold the great majority of the Strand&#39;s listings, so there is always inventory, always comparable sales, and always a buyer when you sell.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want quiet, and I am buying for myself as much as for yield</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/pawleys-island/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Pawleys Island</a>. Higher nightly rates, lower occupancy, an older and higher-end housing stock, and a buyer pool motivated as much by using the place as renting it.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.05rem 0"><div style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.12rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.3rem">I want to be near the water without oceanfront pricing</div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65;margin:0">Start with <a href="/submarkets/garden-city/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">Garden City</a>. The peninsula has ocean on one side and the inlet on the othe