+</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The direct answer</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">What it costs to own a home in Myrtle Beach</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Five lines decide it: the loan payment, property taxes, insurance, HOA dues, and upkeep. Two of them surprise almost everyone who moves here. Property tax on the same house is roughly three times higher when it is not your legal residence. Coastal insurance is often several policies, not one.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;">The calculator below adds all five, using the same Horry County tax math as our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax page</a>. It is planning math, not a quote.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="co-calc"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The calculator</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Your true monthly cost</h2><div style="max-width:680px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:14px;padding:1.5rem"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin-bottom:1rem"><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Purchase price ($)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coPrice" type="number" value="300000" oninput="coCalc()"></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Down payment (%)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coDown" type="number" placeholder="Enter %" oninput="coCalc()"></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Rate (%, from your lender&#39;s quote)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coRate" type="number" step="0.125" placeholder="Your rate" oninput="coCalc()"></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Term (years)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coTerm" type="number" value="30" oninput="coCalc()"></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Location</label><select class="idx-select" id="coLoc" onchange="coCalc()"><option value="254.6|83.4">City of Myrtle Beach</option><option value="221.2|0">North Myrtle Beach</option><option value="214.2|0">Surfside Beach</option><option value="272.5|0">Conway</option><option value="207.3|0">Murrells Inlet / Garden City</option><option value="201.0|0" selected>Unincorporated Horry (Carolina Forest, Socastee, Little River)</option></select></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">How you will own it</label><select class="idx-select" id="coStatus" onchange="coCalc()"><option value="4" selected>My legal residence (4%)</option><option value="6">Second home or rental (6%)</option></select></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Insurance ($/mo, your estimate)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coIns" type="number" value="160" oninput="coCalc()"></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">HOA dues ($/mo)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coHoa" type="number" value="0" oninput="coCalc()"></div><div><label style="display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Upkeep reserve (% of value / yr)</label><input class="idx-input" id="coMaint" type="number" step="0.25" value="1" oninput="coCalc()"></div></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-top:1rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem;color:var(--navy);display:grid;gap:.35rem"><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>Loan payment (principal + interest)</span><strong id="coPI">$0</strong></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>Property taxes</span><strong id="coTax">$0</strong></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>Insurance</span><strong id="coInsOut">$0</strong></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>HOA dues</span><strong id="coHoaOut">$0</strong></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between"><span>Upkeep reserve</span><strong id="coUp">$0</strong></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding-top:.6rem;font-size:1.05rem"><span><strong>True monthly cost</strong></span><strong id="coTotal" style="color:var(--brass)">$0</strong></div></div><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.75rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Tax math mirrors our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax calculator</a>: Horry County&#39;s 2026 certified millage, the Act 388 school exemption on legal residences, and the Myrtle Beach TDF credit. It excludes the 65+ homestead exemption and small special districts. Insurance is your estimate; see <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">coastal insurance costs</a>. Example math for planning, not an offer or quote of credit. Your rate and terms come from your lender.</p></div><script>
+function coCalc(){
+ function v(id){return parseFloat(document.getElementById(id).value)||0;}
+ function fmt(n){return '$'+Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');}
+ var SCHOOL_OPS=109.1,TDF=0.534;
+ var p=v("coPrice"),down=v("coDown"),rate=v("coRate"),term=v("coTerm")||30;
+ var parts=document.getElementById("coLoc").value.split("|"),mills=parseFloat(parts[0]),city=parseFloat(parts[1]);
+ var six=document.getElementById("coStatus").value==="6";
+ var ratio=six?0.06:0.04,m=six?mills:(mills-SCHOOL_OPS);
+ var tax=p*ratio*m/1000;
+ if(!six&&city>0){tax-=p*ratio*city/1000*TDF;}
+ tax=Math.max(0,tax)/12;
+ var loan=p*(1-down/100),r=rate/1200,n=term*12;
+ var pi=r>0?loan*r*Math.pow(1+r,n)/(Math.pow(1+r,n)-1):(n>0?loan/n:0);
+ var up=p*v("coMaint")/100/12,ins=v("coIns"),hoa=v("coHoa");
+ /* No rate or down payment is filled in for the visitor (owner rule: the site never
+    states a rate or a down payment on an owner-occupied page), so the loan line waits
+    for theirs instead of assuming one. */
+ var hasDown=document.getElementById("coDown").value.trim()!=="",hasRate=document.getElementById("coRate").value.trim()!=="";
+ var ask=hasDown&&hasRate?"":"Add "+(hasDown?"your rate":hasRate?"your down payment":"down payment and rate");
+ document.getElementById("coPI").textContent=ask||fmt(pi);
+ document.getElementById("coTax").textContent=fmt(tax);
+ document.getElementById("coInsOut").textContent=fmt(ins);
+ document.getElementById("coHoaOut").textContent=fmt(hoa);
+ document.getElementById("coUp").textContent=fmt(up);
+ document.getElementById("coTotal").textContent=ask||fmt(pi+tax+ins+hoa+up);
+}
+coCalc();
+</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Before you offer</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Two numbers to check before you offer</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">First, the tax status. The previous owner&#39;s bill tells you nothing if their status differs from yours, and the county reassesses when a home sells. The application deadlines and exemptions are on the <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">property tax page</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Second, the insurance quote. Get it during due diligence, not after closing. On a condo, the building&#39;s own master policy also decides whether the building can take a conventional loan, which we explain on the <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">non-warrantable condos page</a>. The pieces and how they stack are on the <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">coastal insurance page</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;">One more difference: a condo usually has a lower purchase price and higher dues, because the dues carry the building insurance and exterior upkeep. A house trades dues for direct costs that arrive all at once, not monthly. What dues include, and whether an association can pay for what is coming, is covered in our <a href="/hoa/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">HOA guide</a>. Whether a condo makes sense at all is covered in <a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">are Myrtle Beach condos a good investment</a>.</p><div style="background:var(--ivory);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem 1.3rem;margin-top:1.8rem;max-width:720px;display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between"><p style="margin:0;color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem;font-weight:600">Want us to look at it for you?</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.7rem;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#lead-form">Send it to an expert</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy)"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;padding:3rem 1.5rem"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.9rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:.8rem">Want the real number on a specific home?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.6);max-width:560px;margin:0 auto 1.6rem;line-height:1.7">Send the address. We run taxes, insurance, dues, and payment for that exact property, free.</p><div style="display:flex;gap:.75rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#lead-form">Send it to an expert</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="tel:+18543332135" style="color:var(--ivory);border-color:rgba(244,239,232,.4)">Call 854.333.2135</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">Cost to own FAQ</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much does it cost to own a home in Myrtle Beach each month?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Add five lines: the loan payment, property taxes, insurance, HOA dues, and upkeep. The mix moves a lot between a condo and a house and between a primary home and a rental, which is what the calculator on this page is for.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What is PITI?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Principal, interest, taxes, and insurance, the four pieces most lenders count in your housing payment. HOA dues and upkeep sit on top of PITI, and on the coast they matter.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How does the calculator figure property taxes?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It uses Horry County's 2026 certified millage for the location you pick and the 4 percent or 6 percent assessment based on how you will own the home. It also applies the Act 388 school exemption for legal residences and the Myrtle Beach TDF credit. It is the same model as our property tax page, where the full detail lives.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What should I enter for insurance?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Your best current estimate for the specific home, because coastal quotes vary widely by distance to water, elevation, and roof age. Wind, hail, and flood can be separate policies. Our coastal insurance page explains the pieces, and quotes during due diligence give you the real number.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is a condo cheaper to own than a house?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Often the purchase price is lower but the HOA dues are higher, because the dues carry the building insurance and exterior upkeep. A house trades dues for direct insurance and maintenance costs. Run both through the calculator before deciding.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">How much should I budget for maintenance?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Budget about 1 percent of the home value a year, more for older homes and salt-air exposure. It is a planning number, not a bill, but the money gets spent eventually.</p></div></div></section>
